# React Router 7 Client Data

`clientLoader` and `clientAction` are browser-only counterparts to `loader` and `action`. Use them when:

- The data lives in `IndexedDB`, `localStorage`, or another browser-only API.
- You want to layer a client cache (SWR, query) on top of a server loader.
- You are in SPA mode (`ssr: false`) and need data fetching on non-root routes.

## Canonical shape

```tsx
import type { Route } from "./+types/profile";

export async function loader({ params }: Route.LoaderArgs) {
  return { profile: await getProfileFromDb(params.id) };
}

export async function clientLoader({ params, serverLoader }: Route.ClientLoaderArgs) {
  const fresh = await fetch(`/api/profile/${params.id}`).then((r) => r.json());
  return { profile: fresh };
}

export async function clientAction({ request }: Route.ClientActionArgs) {
  await fetch("/api/profile", { method: "POST", body: await request.formData() });
  return { ok: true };
}

export default function Profile({ loaderData }: Route.ComponentProps) {
  return <pre>{JSON.stringify(loaderData.profile)}</pre>;
}
```

## Hydration

By default `clientLoader` does NOT run on initial load (the server loader's data is reused). To force it on hydration:

```tsx
export async function clientLoader({ serverLoader }: Route.ClientLoaderArgs) {
  return { profile: await fetchFresh() };
}
clientLoader.hydrate = true as const;

export function HydrateFallback() {
  return <p>Loading profile...</p>;
}
```

`HydrateFallback` is mandatory when `clientLoader.hydrate === true`. Without it v7 throws at hydration.

## SPA mode

```ts
// react-router.config.ts
import type { Config } from "@react-router/dev/config";
export default { ssr: false } satisfies Config;
```

In SPA mode:

- Only `app/root.tsx` may export a server `loader` (used at prerender for the shell).
- All other route data must come from `clientLoader`.
- A server `loader` on a non-root route is a build error.

## Refused patterns

- `import fs from "node:fs"` inside a `clientLoader`. Node built-ins are unresolved in the browser bundle.
- `clientLoader.hydrate = true` without exporting `HydrateFallback`. Throws at hydration.
- Putting auth checks in `clientLoader` instead of the server `loader`. Authenticated content flashes before the redirect.

